// Fix 1 — Repetition penalty 4.0 → 16.0:
//   Malformed/unclosed examples show hundreds of `!` tokens inside spans.
//   `SafeRepetitionPenaltyStep` penalizes tokens already in `generated` by the
//   given amount. After the first `!` token, a -4.0 delta is often insufficient
//   to displace `!` from the top-logit position; -16.0 is much more likely to
//   break the loop on the very next step.
//
// Fix 2 — EOS-rescue inside open spans:
//   When EOS fires during a constrained step while a span is open, the best
//   attempt breaks immediately, leaving `<<` unclosed (9 `final_span_unclosed`
//   cases). Now we call `CloseSpanWithinBudget(remEos)` to find the longest
//   complete prefix reached and emit `>>` before exiting.
//
// Fix 3 — 30-token span-length guard:
//   Valid symbolic expressions are typically 5–20 tokens. If a span grows to 30
//   tokens without reaching `IsCompletePrefix`, a dead loop is almost certain.
//   We force-close via `CloseSpanWithinBudget(remaining)`, which rolls back to
//   the longest complete prefix seen so far and closes cleanly.
//
// All other structure is identical to the best attempt:
//   – Free unconstrained generation with RenderedEndsWith("<<") detection
//   – Immediate close when IsCompletePrefix fires
//   – Budget guard at remaining ≤ closeReserve=80 via CloseSpanWithinBudget
//   – Final cleanup after loop if span is still open
// CSD_RATIONALE_END
// CSD_PROOF_SKETCH_BEGIN
// Invariant 1 — parser_validity:
//   insideConstrainedOut ==> parser.IsValidPrefix(currentConstrainedOut)
//
//   (budget-guard / length-guard / EOS-rescue / final-cleanup — all call CloseSpanWithinBudget):
//     Postcondition: `insideOut ==> parser.IsValidPrefix(currentOut)`.
//     Closed path (ci=false): implication vacuously true. Still-open path: postcondition
//     gives parser.IsValidPrefix(cc) directly. Both preserve the invariant. ✓
//
//   (!insideConstrainedOut branch):
//     If RenderedEndsWith triggers we set currentConstrainedOut := [], which satisfies
//     IsValidPrefix([]) by the method precondition. Otherwise insideConstrainedOut stays
//     false and the implication is vacuous. ✓
//
//   (IsCompletePrefix branch):
//     CloseConstrainedSpan sets insideConstrainedOut := false; implication vacuously true. ✓
//
//   (constrained step, non-EOS):
//     SafeRepetitionPenaltyStep hard-masks to parser-valid tokens plus EOS, so next is
//     parser-valid or EOS. AppendConstrainedToken postcondition: parser.IsValidPrefix(currentOut). ✓
//
// Invariant 2 — progress:
//   |generated| <= |generatedPrefix| + steps
//
//   (budget-guard / length-guard, steps_in, remaining = maxSteps - steps_in):
//     CloseSpanWithinBudget(remaining): |cg| <= |generated| + remaining
//     <= |generatedPrefix| + steps_in + (maxSteps - steps_in) = |generatedPrefix| + maxSteps.
//     After steps := maxSteps: |generated| <= |generatedPrefix| + steps. ✓
//
//   (!insideConstrainedOut): steps += 1; at most one token appended to generated. ✓
//
//   (IsCompletePrefix): steps += 1; CloseConstrainedSpan appends at most one `>>` token. ✓
//
//   (constrained step non-EOS, steps_in):
//     steps := steps_in + 1; AppendConstrainedToken appends exactly one token.
//     |generated| <= |generatedPrefix| + steps_in + 1 = |generatedPrefix| + steps. ✓
//
//   (constrained step EOS-rescue, steps_in):
//     After EOS step (no append): steps = steps_in + 1; |generated| <= |generatedPrefix| + steps_in.
